# Standing demand: push the Standing Echo persistence frontier.
#
# RATCHET LOG (the floor rises each time the swarm meets it — Nick's
# living-demand pattern, ratified 2026-08-07):
#   0.87 → RESOLVED 2026-08-07 by CRY-014468 (persistence 0.875, deep
#          30-generation metamaterial shift, order rs-msibdssh-0) — beat
#          the 0.8679 all-time record after 25 shallow attempts failed.
#   0.88 → RESOLVED 2026-08-07 by CRY-015518 (persistence 0.887, noise
#          tolerance 1.000 — a perfect-tolerance record row; order
#          rs-msj5mz38-0, fell within the first deep 6x30 series).
#   0.90 → RESOLVED 2026-08-07 by CRY-016438 (persistence 0.910, noise
#          tolerance 0.998; order rs-msj5zv2n-0, first deep 6x45 series).
#          Deeper budgets yield bigger jumps: 30 gens ≈ +0.010, 45 gens
#          ≈ +0.023.
#   0.925 → STANDING (the wall, found 2026-08-07). A full deep 6x60
#          series went 0/fulfilled; best it grew was CRY-017105 at
#          0.9125 (+0.002). The budget scaling law COLLAPSED:
#          30 gens ≈ +0.010, 45 gens ≈ +0.023, 60 gens ≈ +0.002 —
#          evolutionary search saturates near persistence ~0.91.
#          Meeting this floor likely needs a SEARCH-STRATEGY change
#          (crystal lane: material physics, fitness shaping, seeding
#          from the 0.91 elite), not more generations. The demand
#          stands: that is what a research frontier is.
#
# This is the KCB-1 research direction (close the delayed-identity gap =
# longer-lived structure) expressed as scheduler demand. Noise-tolerance
# floors are deliberately absent: the registry saturates noise_tolerance
# at 1.0, so persistence is the open frontier. Lesson encoded in the
# worker: depth beats breadth here (KHDL_WORK_GENERATIONS=30).

cell FrontierEcho() {
    when always => base crystal.primitive "Standing Echo" min_persistence 0.925
}

grow FrontierEcho()
